cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "breakingnews: story segmentation for broadcast-news transcripts"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, and see the README for what the accuracy figures do and do not establish."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhalla
    given-names: Sakshi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6803-7657"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshi-bhalla/breakingnews"
url: "https://huggingface.co/sakshib3/Llama-3.1-breakingnews"
# doi: added after the first Zenodo deposit
abstract: >-
  A LoRA adapter on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct that locates the word offsets where
  one story ends and the next begins in a broadcast-news transcript, plus the
  scoring metrics and the segment/merge round trip. Boundaries only: it does not
  label, classify or summarise the resulting segments. Validation F1 0.596 at a
  +/-25-word tolerance on 117 transcripts and 322 boundaries; precision is a
  lower bound rather than an estimate, and every result is single-seed.
keywords:
  - text segmentation
  - broadcast news
  - content analysis
  - LoRA
